    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "dde94ecb18d9831284d67d9eb57d5618b1cc113074b81561344c14672f9ce1bb",
      "text": "A day in the most outstanding places of the Sacred Valley. First, Chinchero, the most typical and colourful village of the valley, famous for its weavers: a short stop at a textile centre reveals the old Inca techniques for dyeing and spinning alpaca wool, before visiting the Inca square and its colonial church. Continue to Moray, an Inca site of concentric agricultural terraces that served as a laboratory to recreate microclimates. Lunch, then Ollantaytambo, often called the last living Inca village, with the Temple of the Ten Windows, the Princess Baths and the Sun Temple. Overnight in the Sacred Valley.\n\nIncluded: Sacred Valley tour · Lunch · Breakfast",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
